BTW, using GCC 3.2 and adding the -Os option, `size
drivers/acpi/built-in.o` drops from 213381 bytes to 174063 bytes (with
everything selected but debug messages).

Big thanks to Andi Kleen to suggesting we try this. I remember Alan Cox
mentioning that size optimizations were coming in gcc 3 -- it's nice to
actually see them.

The next release will build with -Os by default.

Regards -- Andy

